<title>THAILAND: Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Dec 17.</title>
<headline>Thai rice vessels loading and movements at Dec 17.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Thai Commerce Ministry and independent surveyors detailed rice loading at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel		Date of Arrival   Quantity     Destination</p>
<p>Tong Shun	   25/11/96		3,000	  China</p>
<p>But 2		 27/11/96		5,000	  Indonesia</p>
<p>Seacword	    28/11/96	     10,000	  Iran</p>
<p>Fairwinds	   29/11/96		7,500	  Nigeria</p>
<p>Ming Sun	    29/11/96		5,000	  Singapore</p>
<p>An Jiang	    29/11/96		3,000	  China</p>
<p>Gondan Seaway	2/12/96		5,000	  Japan</p>
<p>San Jing	     3/12/96		2,300	  China</p>
<p>Main Rainboow	3/12/96		5,000	  China</p>
<p>Nebula		 3/12/96		1,500	  Malaysia</p>
<p>Suz Dal		4/12/96	     10,000	  Nigeria</p>
<p>Grace Luna	   6/12/96		5,500	  Japan</p>
<p>Dong An		6/12/96		3,000	  China</p>
<p>Tolich		 6/12/96	     13,500	  China</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
